+# Blocked: 002_unique_email on the production snapshot
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`migrations/002_unique_email.sql` can install `users.email NOT NULL` and a
+case-insensitive unique index (`lower(email)`) on a fresh or already-clean
+database. It **cannot be applied to `fixtures/prod_snapshot.sql`** while also
+respecting the rule that the migration must not modify or delete customer rows.
+
+## Why
+
+The production snapshot already violates both new constraints:
+
+| Problem | Rows |
+| --- | --- |
+| `email IS NULL` | id 17 (`Goran Okafor`) |
+| Case-insensitive duplicate (`ana.silva@example.com`) | ids 1, 4 (`Ana.Silva@example.com`), 23 |
+
+Rows 1 and 23 are exact duplicates; row 4 differs only by case.
+
+SQLite cannot attach `NOT NULL` or a unique expression index to data that
+already violates it. The only ways to proceed are to change Support's data:
+
+- set or backfill the NULL email for id 17, and
+- delete, merge, or re-email the rows in the `ana.silva@example.com` set
+  (ids 1, 4, 23).
+
+Doing any of that from a migration would modify or delete customer rows, which
+is out of scope for this change and owned by Support. Silently skipping the
+constraint when dirty data is present would just hide the problem and leave
+production unconstrained, so the migration does not do that.
+
+`test_migrations.test_applies_to_prod_snapshot` therefore cannot pass as
+written: it applies the migration to the snapshot and expects success without
+row changes, which is impossible for the data above.
+
+## Current behaviour
+
+The migration checks for NULLs and case-insensitive duplicates first. If any
+exist it aborts before making any schema change, with:
+
+```
+002_unique_email: users.email contains NULLs or case-insensitive duplicates;
+Support must clean the data before this migration can run
+```
+
+Verified that after the abort all 40 rows in the snapshot are unchanged.
+
+## Unblocking
+
+Support needs to resolve id 17's missing email and the
+`ana.silva@example.com` duplicates (ids 1, 4, 23). Once the snapshot is clean,
+`002_unique_email.sql` applies as-is. The fresh-database test
+(`test_constraint_on_fresh_db`) passes today.
